  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-1",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/34540419",
    "excerpt": "\"DataDog Don't Discount\" - compared to most enterprise vendors it's a lot harder to get a discount from Datadog; price has always been what's on the website.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-13T01:06:15.092Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-2",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/34540419",
    "excerpt": "We spend a few thousand a month with Datadog and our account manager reaches out every quarter to adjust our monthly commit, providing about a 20% discount off website prices.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-13T01:06:15.092Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-3",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/34540419",
    "excerpt": "Datadog's main competitive advantage is correlating data across APM, custom metrics, and logging through tagging, plus built-in Jupyter-style notebooks for incidents and dashboards.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-13T01:06:15.092Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-4",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/34540419",
    "excerpt": "Their data correlation is awful compared to competitors like Honeycomb, Dynatrace and Instana. Users end up sifting through outdated dashboards and notebooks instead of seeing anomalies directly.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-13T01:06:15.092Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-5",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/34540419",
    "excerpt": "I wish Datadog was opinionated and displayed everything in UTC by default. It's insane that software meant to help unfuck production doesn't show timezone by default on logs/metrics.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-13T01:06:15.092Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-6",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/42648043",
    "excerpt": "Datadog was easier to use for everybody, with useful baked-in features like apdex scores, and non-devs could design dashboards. Lost the ~$6M/yr account due to lack of billing transparency and an incompetent account rep who angered finance and embarrassed the CTO.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-13T01:06:15.092Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-7",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/20781610",
    "excerpt": "Datadog solves a real (and burning) problem for product engineering teams, and though expensive, is worth every penny.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-13T01:06:15.092Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-8",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/20781610",
    "excerpt": "Had difficulty with Datadog setup and tracking; execution trace collection was much more resource intensive than New Relic. Support emails went unanswered until a co-worker complained publicly on Twitter.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-13T01:06:15.092Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-9",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/20781610",
    "excerpt": "As a long time Datadog customer, their product has always been amazing, absolutely reliable, and beautifully designed. We never once flinched at our bill.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-13T01:06:15.092Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-10",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=37558357",
    "excerpt": "Used both Datadog and New Relic in large-scale production apps; for the cost, still not very impressed by the DX/UX.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-13T01:06:15.092Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-11",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=37558357",
    "excerpt": "My two Datadog favourite features were: clicking on a field to make it a custom search dimension in another click, and flame graphs. Delicious flame graphs.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-13T01:06:15.092Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-12",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=37558357",
    "excerpt": "Datadog's server hexagon map/chart thingie is something else. The kind of innovation that wins prizes.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-13T01:06:15.092Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-13",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=37558357",
    "excerpt": "Datadog is cool but the price is ridiculously high for small orgs.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-13T01:06:15.092Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-14",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=37558357",
    "excerpt": "Datadog's one of my favorite providers, and their pricing is great for small businesses, but probably unaffordable for larger businesses.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-13T01:06:15.092Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-15",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=33049046",
    "excerpt": "The user interface experience I had with DataDog was definitely reminiscent of something produced from a dog's rear end. Felt like a product where no one in the org said 'no' to an idea, very Atlassian.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-13T01:06:15.092Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-16",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=33049046",
    "excerpt": "I like DataDog but it is prohibitively expensive for monitoring serverless applications, even with negotiated rates. Paying for DataDog is many orders of magnitude higher than our AWS bill.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-13T01:06:15.092Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "datadog-comm-17",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=33049046",
    "excerpt": "Is there any outlier analysis on this? That's a key advantage of DataDog and NewRelic.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-13T01:06:15.092Z"
  },
